From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] linux 7.2: sync the addr shadow before registration

register_netdevice() checks dev_addr against dev_addr_shadow. The
pre-register direct write leaves the shadow zeroed, so the check warns
at module load. Copy the address into both fields while the netdev is
still uninitialized; eth_hw_addr_set() is unsafe there because the
address list does not exist yet.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/include/osdep_service_linux.h
+++ b/include/osdep_service_linux.h
@@ -54,10 +54,12 @@
 
 #if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(5, 17, 0))
 #define rtw_set_netdev_addr(dev, addr) do { \
-	if ((dev)->reg_state == NETREG_UNINITIALIZED) \
+	if ((dev)->reg_state == NETREG_UNINITIALIZED) { \
 		_rtw_memcpy((dev)->dev_addr, (addr), ETH_ALEN); \
-	else \
+		_rtw_memcpy((dev)->dev_addr_shadow, (addr), ETH_ALEN); \
+	} else { \
 		eth_hw_addr_set((dev), (addr)); \
+	} \
 } while (0)
 #else
 #define rtw_set_netdev_addr(dev, addr) _rtw_memcpy((dev)->dev_addr, (addr), ETH_ALEN)
